{# stat_callout — a single REAL figure lifted from the prose into a small
   dark-glass corner card (Richard's "expensive afterthought" weighting that
   chromatically anchors an otherwise text-heavy page). AUGMENT device: the
   figure already lives (and is already counted) in the body copy, so this adds
   visual proof WITHOUT adding text — it never fabricates a number.

   Token-only / brand-agnostic: the dark-glass fill, accent numeral, glow +
   keyline come from tokens via color-mix (Chromium honours the gradient/glow;
   WeasyPrint drops the glow losslessly). The host page positions .c-statcard.

   DATA CONTRACT (diagram dict, kind == "stat_callout"):
     figure : the number string, shown VERBATIM (e.g. "30 %", "15x", "200.000 €")
     label  : optional one-line caption under the figure

   Graceful: no figure → renders nothing. #}
{% macro stat_callout(diagram) %}
{%- if diagram and diagram.kind == 'stat_callout' and diagram.figure -%}
<figure class="c-statcard" role="img"
        aria-label="{{ diagram.figure }} {{ diagram.label or '' }}">
  <span class="c-statcard__figure">{{ diagram.figure }}</span>
  {%- if diagram.label %}<span class="c-statcard__label">{{ diagram.label }}</span>{% endif %}
</figure>
{%- endif -%}
{% endmacro %}
